: true, "raw_response": "{
  "reason": "The current model overfits quickly (best epoch 18 with validation loss 0.1286 vs training 0.0799), uses only RDKit fingerprints without leveraging pretrained molecular embeddings, and has no mechanism to handle the high missing rates (e.g., MGMB 96% missing). Adding ChemBERTa-2 embeddings will provide rich semantic information that fingerprints miss, and implementing uncertainty-weighted loss with task-specific heads will adaptively weight tasks with sparse data, improving generalization.",
