  "module": ["model_design"],
  "plan": {
    "model_design": "Change: Replace per-task gating with a single fingerprint-based gating network (Category: Model Architecture). What: Remove the list of GatingNetworks (one per task) and replace with a single GatingNetwork that takes the fingerprint representation (not the fused encoder output) and produces routing weights for all tasks. The gating network input changes from encoder output (hidden_dim=128) to fingerprint projection (3239→128). The task heads remain but now all tasks share the same expert outputs weighted by the same gate weights. Why: The high missing rates cause some tasks to have very few training samples, making per-task gating unreliable and prone to overfitting. A single gating network based on fingerprints acts as a learnable molecular descriptor that routes each molecule to the most suitable expert for all properties, leveraging the full dataset for training the gating mechanism. This improves generalization for sparse tasks by sharing routing decisions. Implementation: In MoE_MultiTaskModel.__init__, keep self.gate = GatingNetwork(hidden_dim, num_experts) (single gate). In forward, compute gate_weights = self.gate(fingerprints_proj) where fingerprints_proj = F.relu(self.encoder.fingerprint_proj(fingerprints)). Then for each task, multiply the same gate_weights with expert_outputs. Preserve variable names and output shape (batch, num_tasks)."
